+ *  3. On detecting a dead GPU it issues NO further MMIO. Theirs writes the
+ *     invalidate semaphore back on the way out, which is another access to a
+ *     device that just stopped answering -- the exact operation the patch
+ *     exists to avoid. Leaking the semaphore is harmless here: the GPU is gone
+ *     and the next thing that happens is a reset.
+ *
+ * Why all-ones means "gone": a read that never completes on this board's
+ * internal PCIe fabric does not time out, it hangs the CPU. When the fabric
+ * does answer for an absent device, it answers all-ones. Catching that lets us
+ * leave before taking invalidate_lock -- and hanging while holding that
+ * spinlock is a plausible mechanism for the hard host hangs we see, where the
+ * machine dies with nothing in dmesg or the journal.
+ */
+extern int bc250_tlb_trace;   /* definido em amdgpu_vm.c */
